    <!-- Title -->
    <h2>Please Stop Waiting Out Allergy Season Until You Read This. What Nobody Told Me About Natural Allergy Relief and the Morning Habit I Started at 54</h2>

    <div class="vy-dli-byline">
      <img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/vysta/lp-676-betterbrand/images/author.jpg" alt="Marion Ellis, contributor at The Wellness Brief">
      <div class="vy-dli-byline-meta">
        <p class="vy-dli-byline-name">Marion Ellis</p>
        <p class="vy-dli-byline-role">Contributor, The Wellness Brief</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    
    <!-- Hero Image -->
    <div class="vy-dli-image-block">
      <img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/vysta/lp-676-betterbrand/images/img-1.webp" alt="Woman in her fifties standing in her garden with a mug of tea on a spring morning, blossom and grasses behind her">
      <p class="vy-dli-image-caption">Results may vary from person to person</p>
    </div>
    
    <!-- Opening Story -->
    <p><span class="vy-dli-bold-italic">"Until this year, I had never done one thing for my lungs. I know how that sounds coming from a 54-year-old woman."</span></p>

    <p>For years, allergy season was just a stretch of the year I never looked forward to. I knew roughly when it started and roughly when it ended, and in between I carried on and waited for the calendar to turn. What I never did, in all that time, was anything at all for my lungs.</p>

    <p>I kept meaning to look into it properly. One year I bought an air purifier, put it in the living room, and never once changed the filter. That was the entire extent of my planning, and I am being generous calling it planning.</p>

    <p>Eventually I stopped thinking about it as something I could get ahead of.</p>

    <p><span class="vy-dli-bold">Some people are organised about this sort of thing. I wasn&rsquo;t one of them.</span></p>

    <p>Then, at my sister&rsquo;s birthday in February, I got talking to her friend Denise in the kitchen. She is a few years older than me and she gardens all year round, and she mentioned in passing that she takes something for her lungs every morning. Not in spring. Every morning.</p>

    <p>She used to do exactly what I did, which was nothing. Allergy season came, she waited it out, and then she forgot about it until the following year. Then someone said something to her that changed how she thought about the whole thing.</p>

    <p><span class="vy-dli-bold-italic">"You can spend every spring bracing for it, or you can spend the year actually supporting your lungs."</span></p>

    <p>Instead of thinking about her lungs for a few weeks a year and then forgetting them, she started supporting her respiratory health daily, all year, the same way she takes her vitamin D in the morning without giving it any thought.</p>

    <p><span class="vy-dli-italic">"Spring is when you think about your lungs,"</span> she said, <span class="vy-dli-italic">"but it isn&rsquo;t when you should start."</span></p>

    <p>She told me what she actually takes, and it is about as simple as it gets. Two full droppers in eight ounces of water, first thing in the morning, before her coffee. It is alcohol free, which she said matters when you are putting something in a glass of water every day. I was skeptical, mostly because I had spent years doing nothing at all. But two droppers in a glass of water is hardly a commitment, so I ordered a bottle and put it beside the kettle where I would actually see it.</p>

    <p><span class="vy-dli-italic">"This is the one I take. Mullein and chlorophyll, alcohol free, and a pharmacist put the formula together. Two droppers in water, that&rsquo;s it."</span></p>
    
    <!-- Section 2 -->
    <h2>What allergy season actually puts in the air. And why I wanted something plant-based every day</h2>

    <img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/vysta/lp-676-betterbrand/images/img-2.jpg" alt="Wild mullein plants with soft grey-green leaves and yellow flowers growing in a sunny meadow" style="width:100%; height:auto; margin: 20px 0;">
    
    <p>The one I settled on was <a href="https://www.trybetterbrand.com/products/betterlungs%C2%AE-mullein-chlorophyll?variant=50211235954987" class="vy-dli-product-link">BetterLungs&#174; Mullein + Chlorophyll</a>. It is a liquid you mix into water rather than a capsule, which suited me because I have never got on with pills. Two full droppers into 8 oz of water, stir, drink. It comes in Original or Mint, and one bottle covers a month.</p>

    <p>In each serving are <span class="vy-dli-bold">280 mg of Mullein Leaf 10:1 Extract</span> equal to <span class="vy-dli-bold">2,800 mg herbal equivalent</span>, with <span class="vy-dli-bold">100 mg of chlorophyll</span> and <span class="vy-dli-bold">no alcohol at all</span>, and it is <span class="vy-dli-bold">pharmacist-formulated and made in the USA</span>.</p>

    <p>The part that made me keep reading was the mullein. Greek and Roman herbalists were writing about mullein leaf for respiratory support roughly two thousand years ago, and it never really left the herbal cabinet after that. The chlorophyll alongside it is there to support healthy oxygen flow and steady everyday energy. So none of this is new. It is an old plant, in a modern dose, with the amounts printed on the bottle.*</p>

    <p>What sold me was how little it asks of me. No routine to learn, no timing it around food, and nothing in it that counts as an antihistamine or a stimulant. It is daily support against the ordinary stuff in the air, pollen in spring and whatever the traffic outside is adding. Which is why it goes in every morning and not just in April.</p>

    <p>The company behind it helped too. Betterbrand was started by Dr. Chris Jackson, a Doctor of Pharmacy, and every product gets dosed by a pharmacist rather than guessed at. I cannot say that about most of what I have bought over the years.</p>
    
    <!-- Section 3 -->
    <h2>My first few days with it, and the part nobody tells you about supplements</h2>

    <div class="vy-dli-image-block">
      <img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/vysta/lp-676-betterbrand/images/img-3.jpg" alt="Hands adding two droppers of BetterLungs Mullein and Chlorophyll into a glass of water on a kitchen counter">
      <p class="vy-dli-image-caption">Results may vary from person to person</p>
    </div>
    
    <p>Here is the part every glowing review skips: day one is not the story. I ordered a bottle, it turned up on a Thursday, and I put it on the kitchen counter fully expecting it to join the graveyard of half used jars in my cupboard.</p>

    <p>The next morning I squeezed two full droppers into a glass of water and watched it go a deep green. The taste is mild and a little earthy, closer to a herbal tea than anything else. Perfectly drinkable. Not exciting.</p>

    <p>By day two the novelty had worn off, and the skeptic in me thought, right, so this is another one of my phases. I started drafting the message I was going to send my sister about wasting money again.</p>

    <p>I never sent it. Instead I went back and actually read how you are meant to take the stuff.</p>

    <p><span class="vy-dli-italic">"It sounds obvious saying it out loud,"</span> I admitted to her weeks later, <span class="vy-dli-italic">"but I was judging a daily habit after two glasses of water."</span></p>

    <p>What I had missed is that a supplement is a routine you keep, and routines take a while to bed in. Betterbrand says as much: give it about <span class="vy-dli-bold">4 weeks of daily use</span>. Which is fair enough. You would give anything that long before deciding whether it earns its place on the counter, and the routine is hardly demanding, just <span class="vy-dli-bold">two full droppers in 8 oz of water</span>.*</p>

    <p>You can also take it straight under the tongue if you want it absorbed faster, though I never bothered. Water and a spoon, every morning, and the routine was settled. Four weeks is guidance about the habit, and nothing more than that.*</p>

    <p><span class="vy-dli-bold-italic">Nobody puts that on the front of the box. If they did, I think fewer women would abandon a bottle after two days the way I nearly did.</span></p>

    <p>So I kept going. Two droppers in a glass while the coffee brewed, every morning, and by about the third day I had stopped needing to remember it. It became one of those things my hands do while my brain is still catching up.</p>

    <p><span class="vy-dli-bold">Turns out the habit was the easy part.</span></p>

    <p>By the end of the second week it had stopped feeling like a new thing at all, and honestly that was the bit that caught me off guard.</p>
    
    <!-- Section 4 -->
    <h2>Two droppers, one glass of water, and the other way to do it</h2>

    <div class="vy-dli-image-block">
      <img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/vysta/lp-676-betterbrand/images/img-4.jpg" alt="An open hand holding two lung-shaped BetterLungs Mullein Gummies beside the pear flavored pouch">
    </div>
    
    <p>Before I get to the habit part, the mechanics, because I had questions about those too. The bit you do takes about fifteen seconds: shake the bottle, squeeze two full droppers into 8 oz of water, drink it. You can also put the two droppers straight under your tongue if you want it absorbed faster, which is what I do on the mornings I am already behind. It is alcohol free, so there is none of that sharp bite you brace for.</p>

    <p>The format is the part people overthink, according to <a href="https://www.trybetterbrand.com/products/betterlungs%C2%AE-mullein-chlorophyll?variant=50211235954987" class="vy-dli-product-link">Betterbrand</a>.</p>

    <p><span class="vy-dli-italic">The tincture is the one to pick if you like a morning glass of water. Two full droppers gives you 280 mg of Mullein Leaf 10:1 Extract, a 2,800 mg herbal equivalent, plus 100 mg of chlorophyll, in Original or Mint.</span> The gummies are the same herb in a form that lives in a handbag. Chew two a day, before or after food, no water needed, and a serving gives you 2,000 mg of mullein leaf extract. They taste like pear, they are shaped like little lungs, and sixty of them is a thirty day supply. <span class="vy-dli-italic">Two formats of one herb sounds like an upsell until you realise the only one worth buying is the one you will still be taking in March.</span></p>

    <p>That answered the question I bring to every supplement before I can even get it out. No antihistamines in it and no stimulants, and no alcohol either. It is pharmacist formulated and made in the USA, by a founder who is a Doctor of Pharmacy, which is more than I can say for most of what I have bought over the years.</p>

    <p>In practice it took no thought at all. Kettle on, two droppers in the glass, drink it while the toast is in the toaster. By the end of the first week I had stopped deciding about it in the morning and just did it.</p>

    <p><span class="vy-dli-bold-italic">It was a Thursday. I got to the bottom of the glass and realised I had no memory of filling it, which is not a thing I would have predicted about myself.*</span></p>

    <p>I want to be careful here, because I have started enough things in January to distrust my own enthusiasm. A drawer of vitamins. A water bottle with the hours printed down the side. Two apps I deleted.</p>

    <p>But it kept happening. Over the next few mornings the bottle migrated from the cupboard to the counter, and then to the spot right beside the kettle where I could not miss it.*</p>

    <p><span class="vy-dli-bold">Nothing dramatic. Nothing anyone coming round would even notice. Just a bottle that had quietly become part of breakfast.</span></p>

    <p>It lines up with how Betterbrand talks about the range, which is that it is built to be taken every day rather than reached for now and then. A bottle is a month, and you are meant to get through it.*</p>

    <p><span class="vy-dli-bold-italic">It was the first spring in a long time that I went into feeling prepared instead of resigned.</span></p>
    
    <!-- Section 5 -->
    <h2>The morning I stopped deciding about it</h2>

    <div class="vy-dli-image-block">
      <img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/vysta/lp-676-betterbrand/images/img-5.webp" alt="The BetterLungs dropper bottle standing beside the kettle on a kitchen counter in the morning">
      <p class="vy-dli-image-caption">Results may vary from person to person</p>
    </div>
    
    <p>The habit didn&rsquo;t announce itself. Somewhere in week three I noticed I had filled the glass and drunk it while reading something on my phone, with no part of me weighing up whether I could be bothered.</p>

    <p>Then it kept going. Mornings at home. A morning at my sister's. One morning in a hotel where I had packed the gummies instead, because measuring droppers over a hotel sink was never going to happen.*</p>

    <p><span class="vy-dli-italic">"That is twenty one days."</span> I said it out loud, alone in my kitchen, counting back from the day the box arrived. <span class="vy-dli-italic">"I have not missed one."</span></p>
    
    <p>My husband still has no idea any of this is going on. It is not a secret, it just never came up, because there is nothing to announce. I fill a glass, I drink it, I put the bottle back by the kettle.</p>

    <p>The thing that surprised me most was how boring it got. A Saturday in March, house quiet, and I filled the glass while the kettle was coming up to the boil without once weighing up whether it was worth it. That is the whole trick as far as I can tell. It stopped being a decision I made every morning and turned into part of making breakfast.</p>

    <p><span class="vy-dli-bold">I got to the end of that week and couldn&rsquo;t tell you which mornings I had taken it, only that I had.</span></p>

    <p><span class="vy-dli-italic">"It&rsquo;s just a glass of water,"</span> I know. <span class="vy-dli-bold-italic">"But I had never once done anything for my lungs in fifty four years, and now I do it before I have even sat down."</span></p>

    <p>The change is not in me, it is in what my mornings look like. I am doing something for my respiratory health every day, and I know I am doing it.</p>

    <p>Because that is why women my age keep buying things and abandoning them in a drawer. Not for the fun of owning another bottle. For the quiet reassurance of knowing you did something ahead of the season instead of standing there in April bracing for it.</p>

    <p>That is what <a href="https://www.trybetterbrand.com/products/betterlungs%C2%AE-mullein-chlorophyll?variant=50211235954987" class="vy-dli-product-link">BetterLungs&#174;</a> ended up giving me, a thing I do every morning without having to talk myself into it.</p>
    
    <!-- Section 6 -->
    <h2>Why I kept it up, and why I started telling people</h2>

    <div class="vy-dli-image-block">
      <img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/vysta/lp-676-betterbrand/images/img-6.jpg" alt="Two women in their fifties talking over mugs of tea at a kitchen table">
      <p class="vy-dli-image-caption">Results may vary from person to person</p>
    </div>
    
    <p>By week four it had stopped being something I had to decide on. Two full droppers in a glass of water while the kettle boils, daily support for my lungs against the everyday environmental stressors I cannot do much about.* The bottle just lives next to the coffee now.</p>

    <p>Near the end of that month I had dinner at my sister&rsquo;s. She is the sort of person who reads the label on everything in your kitchen, so it took her about four minutes.</p>

    <p><span class="vy-dli-italic">"What is this? Since when do you take anything?"</span> she asked, holding the bottle up to the light and reading the back of it like a woman looking for a catch. She did not find one.</p>

    <p>So I told her what it actually is. A plant-based dietary supplement, mullein leaf and chlorophyll, taken every morning for daily respiratory support.*</p>

    <p><span class="vy-dli-bold-italic">"I picked this one because a pharmacist formulated it,"</span> is the short version I gave her. <span class="vy-dli-bold-italic">"The founder is a Doctor of Pharmacy, and the dose is printed on the bottle."</span></p>

    <p>Then she wanted to know what the numbers on the back meant. Mullein Leaf 10:1 Extract, 280 mg per serving, which works out to a 2,800 mg herbal equivalent, plus 100 mg of chlorophyll for healthy oxygen flow and steady everyday energy.*</p>

    <p>She kept turning it over, reading the label out loud. Alcohol free. Made in the USA. One month supply. She asked whether it tasted like a field, and it does not, or at least the mint one does not.</p>

    <p><span class="vy-dli-bold-italic">She ordered one before I left.</span></p>

    <p>That dinner is when I decided to write this. Nobody asked me to. I did it because I spent about fifteen years doing precisely nothing for my lungs, bracing for allergy season every spring like it was weather I had no say in, and I know plenty of women my age who do exactly the same. Starting a daily habit that supports respiratory health was not complicated, and I wish I had got round to it years ago.*</p>

    <p><span class="vy-dli-italic">"The point was never to have something to talk about,"</span> if I am honest. <span class="vy-dli-bold-italic">"It was to stop putting my lungs at the bottom of the list every single year."</span></p>

    <p>So if you are in your fifties and you have never once done anything for your respiratory health, that is why a stranger is telling you about two droppers in a glass of water. It may be worth reading the rest before allergy season starts without you.</p>
    
    <!-- Section 7 - Formula -->
    <h2>Why I settled on this one and stopped shopping around</h2>

    <img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/vysta/lp-676-betterbrand/images/img-7.webp" alt="Overhead flat lay of the BetterLungs Mullein and Chlorophyll bottle with fresh mullein leaves and a glass of water" style="width:100%; height:auto; margin: 20px 0;">
    
    <p>Here is what I found once I actually read up on it. Mullein is not new. People have used the leaf for respiratory support for centuries, and you can trace it back through Greek and Roman herbal medicine, which is a lot longer than anything else in my kitchen cupboard can claim. What is new is having it in a form I would actually take every morning without thinking about it.</p>

    <p><span class="vy-dli-bold">The plant was never the hard part. Remembering to take it every day was.</span></p>

    <p>The tincture is Mullein Leaf 10:1 Extract at 280 mg a serving, a 2,800 mg herbal equivalent, with 100 mg of chlorophyll alongside it, alcohol free, taken as two full droppers in 8 oz of water. Four things convinced me.</p>

    <p><span class="vy-dli-bold">A pharmacist formulated it*:</span> Betterbrand was founded by Dr. Chris Jackson, a Doctor of Pharmacy, and a pharmacist researches and doses every product in the range instead of a marketing team. The mullein and the chlorophyll are in there to support normal lung function and healthy oxygen flow, and nothing else is in there to bulk out the bottle.*</p>

    <p><span class="vy-dli-bold">The dose is printed on the front*:</span> Mullein Leaf 10:1 Extract, 280 mg per serving, which is a 2,800 mg herbal equivalent, and 100 mg of chlorophyll. Alcohol free, made in the USA. I have bought plenty of supplements that hid behind the words proprietary blend, and I would rather read a number than a word.</p>

    <p><span class="vy-dli-bold">You will actually keep taking it:</span> this was my hangup, because I have quit every supplement I ever bought by roughly day nine. Two droppers in a glass of water takes ten seconds. If you would rather chew something there are pear flavored gummies, two a day, and you do not need water for those. It is HSA and FSA eligible as well, which saves an average of 30%. A routine you find annoying is a routine you drop.</p>

    <p><span class="vy-dli-bold">They give you a year to decide*:</span> the 365-Day Guarantee is what made me stop deliberating and just order one. A year is an unusual amount of time to be given, and it is long enough to work out whether daily respiratory support has earned a permanent spot on the kitchen counter or not.*</p>

    <p>Instead of arriving at spring having done nothing about it again, you fill two droppers, tip them into a glass of water and drink it while the kettle boils.* Every morning. That is the whole routine.</p>
    
    <!-- Section 8 - Real Results -->
    <h2>Real People, Real Reviews.</h2>
    
    <p>I am not the only person who has made this a daily habit. These are verified reviews left by other buyers on the <a href="https://www.trybetterbrand.com/products/betterlungs%C2%AE-mullein-chlorophyll?variant=50211235954987" class="vy-dli-product-link">BetterLungs product page</a>, pasted across exactly as written, wobbly punctuation and all.*</p>

    <p>That is the kind of feedback I trust. None of them are making a big claim. They are people who liked what they bought and kept reordering it, which tells you more about something you take every day than any polished paragraph does.</p>
    
